{"schema":1,"fm":{"schema":1,"id":"film-club-track","kind":"workflow","title":"Film club season track","description":"Plans and runs a season of a film club or film society, from theme and programme to a spoken introduction and discussion questions for each screening and an end-of-season review.","category":"media-and-fandom","version":"1.0.0","status":"incubating","stage":["plan","build","review"],"role":["individual","teacher","student"],"requires":["none"],"inputs":["text","preferences"],"output":["plan","script","questions","summary"],"risk":"read-only","invocation":"user","effort":"deep","interaction":"interactive","model_tier":"frontier","reasoning":"recommended","level":"intermediate","depth":"specific","tags":["film-club","film-society","screening-programme","discussion-questions","community-screenings"],"pairs_with":{"prompts":["explore-directors-filmography","explore-national-cinema","plan-movie-marathon","pick-movie-for-group"],"personas":["film-and-book-critic"]},"args":[{"name":"club","description":"Who the club is for and how it runs, for example \"12 neighbours, monthly in a community hall, mixed ages, mostly casual viewers\" or \"school film club, ages 15 to 17\".","type":"text","required":true},{"name":"season","description":"Number of screenings and how long each evening can be, for example \"6 films, monthly, 2.5 hours including discussion\".","type":"string","required":true},{"name":"ideas","description":"Optional themes, films or directors members suggested, and anything already shown.","type":"text"}],"steps":[{"id":"programme","file":"steps/01-programme.md","stage":"plan","gate":"approve"},{"id":"screening-night","file":"steps/02-screening-night.md","stage":"build","gate":"approve"},{"id":"season-review","file":"steps/03-season-review.md","stage":"review","gate":"none"}],"authorship":"ai-assisted","authors":["gabrielanhaia"],"last_reviewed":"2026-10-11","changelog":[{"version":"1.0.0","note":"First version."}]},"body":"Takes a film club through one season as an experienced programmer would: a themed programme, a short introduction and discussion plan for each night, and a review at the end.\n\n<club>\n{{club}}\n</club>\n<season>\n{{season}}\n</season>\n{{#ideas}}<ideas>\n{{ideas}}\n</ideas>{{/ideas}}\n\nEach step produces one artifact and stops for approval or edits. Step 2 repeats once per screening, on request. Step 3 runs after the season.\n\nThroughout:\n- Only real films, with correct directors and years; mark anything uncertain \"(check)\" and prefer a shorter list to a wrong one.\n- Screening rights and licences vary by country and venue; remind me once to check what a public or ticketed screening needs, and never claim a film is cleared or free to show.\n- No spoilers in anything meant to be said before a film; discussion material after the film may discuss everything.","steps":[{"id":"programme","file":"steps/01-programme.md","stage":"plan","gate":"approve","text":"# Step 1: Season programme\n\nDesign the season before any single night.\n\n1. If the audience, the number of screenings or the time per evening is missing, ask up to three questions in one message, then stop.\n2. Propose two or three possible themes that suit this audience (a director, a country, a genre, a decade, a question such as \"films about work\"), each with one line on why it would hold a season together. Use members' ideas where they fit.\n3. For the theme you recommend, build the programme: one film per screening, ordered so the season opens with an accessible film and builds, with variety in era, country and tone, and at least one film by a woman director where you can name one confidently.\n4. For each film: title, director, year, runtime, a one-line spoiler-free pitch, a content note for the audience, and a check that runtime plus discussion fits the evening.\n5. Name one reserve film in case a title cannot be shown.\n\nOutput: a programme table (Night | Film | Director (year) | Runtime | Pitch | Content note), the theme in two sentences, and the reserve.\n\nStop and wait for approval or edits."},{"id":"screening-night","file":"steps/02-screening-night.md","stage":"build","gate":"approve","text":"# Step 2: Screening night pack\n\nPrepare one night from the approved programme. Ask which night if it is not clear.\n\n1. Introduction to read aloud before the film, at most two minutes when spoken: why this film is in the season, one or two things to watch for, context the audience needs, and nothing about the plot beyond the premise.\n2. Discussion plan for after the film, fitted to the time available: one easy opening question anyone can answer, four to six deeper questions moving from reactions to craft to meaning, and one question linking it to earlier films in the season.\n3. Two or three facts about the making of the film that you are confident about, for the host to drop in if talk slows. Mark anything unsure \"(check)\" or leave it out.\n4. A short hosting note: how to bring in quiet members, and how to handle disagreement or a film people disliked.\n\nOutput: Introduction, Discussion questions, Facts for the host, Hosting note.\n\nStop. Offer the next night's pack when I am ready."},{"id":"season-review","file":"steps/03-season-review.md","stage":"review","gate":"none","text":"# Step 3: Season review\n\nRun this after the last screening. Ask me for attendance per night, which films and discussions worked, and any member feedback, then stop until I answer.\n\n1. Summarise the season from what I report: attendance trend, best-received films and discussions, and what fell flat. Use only my information.\n2. Find patterns: lengths, eras, genres or discussion formats that worked better for this group.\n3. Suggest three changes for next season and two or three theme ideas that follow from what worked.\n4. Draft a short thank-you message to members with next season's dates as placeholders.\n\nOutput: Season summary, What worked, Changes, Next themes, Message to members."}]}
